From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hero Siege Offline Toolkit <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Name the Hero Siege patch series in the log

Why: The AurieCore.dll this toolkit distributes stops being upstream's
binary with this series, and a log has to say which build wrote it. One
line straight after upstream's "loaded at" line names the upstream
version and this series' revision, so an aurie.log from a player can
always be matched to the patch series, and through it to the source,
that produced the DLL. The YYToolkit series does the same in its first
log line; the provenance problem that line answers there (a distributed
binary whose changes no document listed) is the one this line prevents
here.

Evidence: Upstream v2.0.2 writes "Aurie Core v2.0.2 loaded at <address>"
as the first line of <game>\bin\aurie.log and nothing that tells an
upstream build from a modified one (read 2026-10-06). The revision string
compiled here is the "series_revision" of third_party/aurie/upstream.json
in hero-siege-offline-toolkit; tests/test_aurie_patch_series.py there
fails when the two differ.

Fails-safe: One informational log line, written after the logger exists
and before any module loads. It reads three compile-time version macros
and a string constant, and changes nothing Aurie does.

Log-markers: "Hero Siege patch series", "(hero-siege-offline-toolkit, third_party/aurie)"

Upstream-status: not submitted. The line identifies a Hero Siege
distribution and has no use upstream.

diff --git a/Aurie/source/AurieMain.cpp b/Aurie/source/AurieMain.cpp
index dbddf56..37be18e 100644
--- a/Aurie/source/AurieMain.cpp
+++ b/Aurie/source/AurieMain.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,11 @@
 
 #include "framework/framework.hpp"
 
+// Hero Siege patch series: the revision of the series this DLL was built from. It must equal
+// "series_revision" in third_party/aurie/upstream.json of hero-siege-offline-toolkit; that
+// repository's tests/test_aurie_patch_series.py compares the two.
+static const char* const g_HeroSiegeSeriesRevision = "hs.1";
+
 // Unload routine, frees everything properly
 static void ArProcessDetach(HINSTANCE)
 {
@@ -125,6 +130,17 @@ static void ArProcessAttach(HINSTANCE Instance)
 
 	DbgPrintEx(LOG_SEVERITY_TRACE, "Aurie Core v%d.%d.%d loaded at %p", AURIE_FWK_MAJOR, AURIE_FWK_MINOR, AURIE_FWK_PATCH, Instance);
 
+	// Hero Siege patch series: name the source of this build, so that an aurie.log can always be
+	// matched to the patch series that produced the DLL which wrote it.
+	DbgPrintEx(
+		LOG_SEVERITY_INFO,
+		"[hs] Aurie Core %d.%d.%d, Hero Siege patch series %s (hero-siege-offline-toolkit, third_party/aurie)",
+		AURIE_FWK_MAJOR,
+		AURIE_FWK_MINOR,
+		AURIE_FWK_PATCH,
+		g_HeroSiegeSeriesRevision
+	);
+
 	LPWSTR command_line = GetCommandLineW();
 	if (wcsstr(command_line, L"-aurie_wait_for_debug"))
 	{
